{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"type-alias-baseatoms-all","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Alias: BaseAtoms_All"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type BaseAtoms_All = { [K in keyof TableState_All]?: Atom<Exclude<TableState_All[K], undefined>> };","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts#L78","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts:78"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internal \"all features\" flat variants of the atom types. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Table_Internal"},{"type":"text","value":"\nuses these so feature code (written generically over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":") can access\nany slice atom (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.columnPinning"},{"type":"text","value":") without TypeScript\nnarrowing away slices that aren't in the current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" union."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keys are optional: feature code can read atoms from slices it doesn't own,\nbut those slices may not be registered on the current table. Consumers must\nuse optional chaining ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.atoms.columnPinning?.get() ?? default"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-alias-baseatoms-all","text":"Type Alias: BaseAtoms_All","level":1}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Type Alias: BaseAtoms\\_All\n\n```ts\ntype BaseAtoms_All = { [K in keyof TableState_All]?: Atom<Exclude<TableState_All[K], undefined>> };\n```\n\nDefined in: [core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts:78](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts#L78)\n\nInternal \"all features\" flat variants of the atom types. `Table_Internal`\nuses these so feature code (written generically over `TFeatures`) can access\nany slice atom (e.g. `table.atoms.columnPinning`) without TypeScript\nnarrowing away slices that aren't in the current `TFeatures` union.\n\nKeys are optional: feature code can read atoms from slices it doesn't own,\nbut those slices may not be registered on the current table. Consumers must\nuse optional chaining (`table.atoms.columnPinning?.get() ?? default`).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: BaseAtoms_All\ntitle: BaseAtoms_All\n---\n\n# Type Alias: BaseAtoms\\_All\n\n```ts\ntype BaseAtoms_All = { [K in keyof TableState_All]?: Atom<Exclude<TableState_All[K], undefined>> };\n```\n\nDefined in: [core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts:78](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/core/table/coreTablesFeature.types.ts#L78)\n\nInternal \"all features\" flat variants of the atom types. `Table_Internal`\nuses these so feature code (written generically over `TFeatures`) can access\nany slice atom (e.g. `table.atoms.columnPinning`) without TypeScript\nnarrowing away slices that aren't in the current `TFeatures` union.\n\nKeys are optional: feature code can read atoms from slices it doesn't own,\nbut those slices may not be registered on the current table. Consumers must\nuse optional chaining (`table.atoms.columnPinning?.get() ?? default`).\n"}
